    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2). Here's what I changed to implement the redesigned identity key.\n\n## Summary\n\n**New identity key** \u2014 `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))`:\n- Added `model/Soundex.java` \u2014 standard American Soundex (letter + 3 digits, H/W transparent, `\"0000\"` for no letters).\n- Rewrote `model/IdentityKey.of()` to hash `telephone|email|soundex(lastName)` via the existing `Sha256.hex` (telephone is already E.164-normalized and email already lower-cased by `ValidateOwnerFields`), yielding a 64-char hex string.\n\n**Duplicate detection (409) now keyed on the single identity key:**\n- Rewrote `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` to reject when `IdentityKey.of(newOwner)` equals an existing **non-deleted** owner's key. Dropped the old `householdId`/`sharesHousehold` household-duplicate logic per the spec.\n- **Wired it into the pipeline** \u2014 it existed as a class but was never referenced in `owners.POST.yml`; added a `checkIdentity` step after `build`, before `assignHousehold`. The email-domain blocklist still runs first (it's in the earlier `validate` step, a 400).\n- Updated `OwnerIdentityConflictException` to carry/report the `identityKey`.\n\n**Soft-match redesigned** \u2014 `AssignPossibleDuplicate` now flags when `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` both match (non-deleted, lowest id, null postcode never matches). So two owners with the same last name + postcode but different telephones are now created as a soft match rather than a hard 409.\n\n**Docs kept in sync:** updated `openapi.yml` (`identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, and the now-inert `sharesHousehold`) and the stale Javadoc/YAML comments in `AssignHousehold` and the POST pipeline.\n\n`householdId` itself is retained \u2014 it's still used for household sizing/membership/customer-code \u2014 it's just no longer the basis for 409.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec says duplicate detection is \"now the single identity key\" and doesn't mention `sharesHousehold`, so I made that flag a no-op (documented as retained for compatibility) rather than removing the request field. No tests exercise it either way.",
